<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Portable Memory + Search core (Phase 3 · Windows port · memory-search lane).

    This is the Windows peer of the macOS semantic-search + memory-extraction engine:
      Search:
        AgentLens/Services/Search/VectorSearch/VectorSemanticProvider.swift  (cosine top-k)
        AgentLens/Services/Search/VectorSearch/VectorIndexTypes.swift        (vector types)
        AgentLens/Services/Search/SearchService+Ranking.swift                (score fusion / RRF)
        AgentLens/Services/Search/Embedding/EmbeddingProviderProtocol.swift  (embedding seam)
        AgentLens/Services/Search/Embedding/DeterministicEmbeddingProviders.swift (hash embed)
        AgentLens/Services/Search/RetrievalHealthService.swift               (health status math)
      Memory:
        AgentLens/Services/Memory/MemoryExtractionPromptBuilder.swift        (prompt template)
        AgentLens/Services/Memory/MemoryExtractionPolicy.swift               (accept/reject rules)
        AgentLens/Services/Memory/MemoryRecallBudget.swift                   (recall budget math)
        AgentLens/Services/Memory/MemoryExtractionParser.swift               (LLM response parse)
        AgentLens/Services/Memory/MemoryExtractionLLMClient.swift            (LLM seam)
        OpenBurnBarCore/.../Memory/MemorySecretPIIGate.swift                 (secret/PII gate)

    It targets plain net8.0 — NO Windows TFM, zero P/Invoke, zero UI framework, zero
    network client — on purpose: the SAME managed assembly the WinUI shell
    (net8.0-windows) links is unit-tested on the macOS authoring host today
    (`dotnet test`). Mirrors the already-proven OpenBurnBar.App.TextExpansion /
    OpenBurnBar.App.Settings portable-core pattern: a higher-runtime test project
    (net10.0) references this net8.0 library, and the WinUI app references it too.

    The REAL embedding + memory-extraction NETWORK calls (OpenAI embeddings, the
    Claude/OpenAI memory-extraction LLM) are the OS/network adapter and are explicitly
    DEFERRED to bucket B. They plug in behind the seams defined here:
      • IEmbeddingProvider          — text -> float[] embedding (network in prod)
      • ICrossEncoderScorer         — (query, candidate) -> relevance score (network in prod)
      • IMemoryExtractionLlmClient  — prompt -> raw completion JSON (network in prod)
      • the injected clock (Func&lt;DateTimeOffset&gt;) — deadlines / staleness windows
    Everything above those seams — cosine/dot similarity, top-k ranking, score fusion,
    the deterministic hash embedding, retrieval-health status classification, the
    prompt template, the accept/reject policy, the recall-budget math, the response
    parser, and the secret/PII gate — is PORTABLE and carries real xUnit coverage in
    windows/tests/memory-search/.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net8.0</TargetFramework>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <RootNamespace>OpenBurnBar.App.MemorySearch</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>OpenBurnBar.App.MemorySearch</AssemblyName>
    <!--
      Lets the net8.0 library be RESTORED/BUILT by the net10.0 SDK on macOS without
      a Windows targeting pack. It is a pure managed library, so no Windows facet
      is needed; this simply keeps tooling quiet on the authoring host.
    -->
    <EnableWindowsTargeting>true</EnableWindowsTargeting>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!--
      Link (do NOT duplicate) the committed secret/PII corpus as an embedded resource so the gate
      loads the SAME bytes the macOS/daemon gate loads — single source of truth,
      OpenBurnBarCore/Sources/OpenBurnBarCore/Resources/secret-pattern-corpus.json. It is text (JSON),
      so it does not trip the no-tracked-binaries tripwire, and it lives outside windows/ so it is not
      counted by the Windows tree-size budget. MemoryGateCorpus.LoadEmbedded resolves it by the
      LogicalName suffix.
    -->
    <EmbeddedResource Include="../../../OpenBurnBarCore/Sources/OpenBurnBarCore/Resources/secret-pattern-corpus.json">
      <LogicalName>OpenBurnBar.App.MemorySearch.secret-pattern-corpus.json</LogicalName>
    </EmbeddedResource>
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
